### Sattadhar Textile — Credit at the counter + bill editing with a paper trail
### VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Run top to bottom.
###
### Two things are being demonstrated:
###   · a credit sale to a walk-in in ONE request — no detour through the
###     customer form, which is what the counter complained about;
###   · an edit that changes the bill without rewriting any ledger, and that
###     an owner can see afterwards.

@base = http://localhost:4000
@api = {{base}}/api/v1

### ─── 1. Login as ADMIN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "ChangeMe@123" }

###
@adminAccess = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ─── 2. Login as STAFF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
### kirti is seeded WITHOUT `bill.edit` — step 6 must fail before step 7
### turns it on. That failure is the point of running this in order.
# @name staffLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "kirti", "password": "Staff@123" }

###
@staffAccess = {{staffLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ─── 3. Pick a product with stock ──────────────────────────────────────
# @name products
GET {{api}}/products?pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

###
@productId = {{products.response.body.data.items[0].id}}

### ─── 4. Credit sale to a walk-in, in one request ───────────────────────
### No customerId. The phone number is enough: the customer is registered
### inside this transaction and the ₹900 lands on their khata.
###   → 201, walkInCustomer.outcome = "registered", dueAmount = 900
# @name bill
POST {{api}}/bills
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "billingMode": "NON_GST",
  "walkInName": "Raghav Bhai",
  "walkInPhone": "98250 41122",
  "paymentMode": "CREDIT",
  "paidAmount": 100,
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 5, "rate": 200 }]
}

###
@billId = {{bill.response.body.data.id}}
@customerId = {{bill.response.body.data.walkInCustomer.customerId}}

### ─── 5. The khata already knows ────────────────────────────────────────
###   → outstanding 900, one CREDIT_SALE entry
GET {{api}}/ledger/customer/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 6. Staff tries to edit WITHOUT the permission ─────────────────────
###   → 403 FORBIDDEN. Editing is off by default; rewriting a bill after it
###     has been handed over is the easiest way to cover a mistake.
PATCH {{api}}/bills/{{billId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "trying it on", "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1, "rate": 200 }] }

### ─── 7. Owner turns `bill.edit` on for that account ────────────────────
### No API for this yet — do it in the app (More → Staff) or directly:
###   UPDATE users SET permissions = permissions || '{"bill.edit": true}'
###   WHERE username = 'kirti';
### Then re-run step 2 to get a token carrying the new permission.

### ─── 8. Now the edit lands ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### Customer took 2 metres less. `items` is the complete new line list.
###   → 200, grandTotal 600, paidAmount still 100, dueAmount 500,
###     revisionCount 1, billNumber UNCHANGED
PATCH {{api}}/bills/{{billId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Customer took 2 metres less",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 3, "rate": 200 }]
}

### ─── 9. Stock came back as a NEW movement ──────────────────────────────
###   → newest row is SALE_RETURN qty 2. The original SALE:-5 is untouched,
###     so the product's history still replays exactly.
GET {{api}}/stock/movements?productId={{productId}}&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 10. The khata moved by a NEW entry ────────────────────────────────
###   → newest is CREDIT_NOTE 400 @ balanceAfter 500, and the original
###     CREDIT_SALE still says balanceAfter 900. Nothing was rewritten.
GET {{api}}/ledger/customer/{{customerId}}?sort=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 11. This bill's history ───────────────────────────────────────────
###   → reason, amountDelta -400, changes[] naming the product and the
###     quantity that moved, and who did it.
GET {{api}}/bills/{{billId}}/revisions
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

### ─── 12. Staff cannot read the shop-wide log ───────────────────────────
###   → 403. "Who has been rewriting bills" is a supervision question, and a
###     supervision report the supervised can read is not one.
GET {{api}}/bills/revisions
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

### ─── 13. The owner can ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
###   → every edit across the shop, newest first. Add &changedById= to
###     narrow it to one staff account.
GET {{api}}/bills/revisions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 14. Cannot revise below money already received ────────────────────
###   → 400: "Rs 100.00 has already been received against this bill…
###     Raise a credit note for the difference instead."
PATCH {{api}}/bills/{{billId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "trying to go below what was paid", "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1, "rate": 10 }] }

### ─── 15. An edit needs a reason ────────────────────────────────────────
###   → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR on `reason`. An unexplained edit reads as
###     tampering, so the schema will not store one.
PATCH {{api}}/bills/{{billId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 3, "rate": 200 }] }

### ─── 16. The same number again is MATCHED, not duplicated ──────────────
###   → walkInCustomer.outcome = "matched", same customerId as step 4
POST {{api}}/bills
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "billingMode": "NON_GST",
  "walkInName": "Raghav Bhai",
  "walkInPhone": "+919825041122",
  "paymentMode": "CASH",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1, "rate": 200 }]
}
